{
	"_comment": "Attribute sets and the CSS each side must produce. Read by tests/js/block-styles.test.js and tests/php/Paypal_Payment_Buttons_Test.php, so a value one language drops fails a test in the other. textCases run three times on the PHP side — as the QR caption, the payment link and the button face — because one helper serves all three, and a branch that forgets to call it would otherwise pass. rejected* are values the published page refuses; the canvas has to refuse them too, or a block pasted in code view renders in the editor and disappears on publish. buttonCases are the button's own: its background, its width and border going on the button rather than the card, and the Outline style dropping the background so an inline declaration cannot beat the stylesheet.",
	"cases": [
		{
			"name": "a spacing preset",
			"attributes": {
				"style": {
					"spacing": {
						"margin": {
							"top": "var:preset|spacing|50"
						}
					}
				}
			},
			"declarations": {
				"margin-top": "var(--wp--preset--spacing--50)"
			}
		},
		{
			"name": "zero margin cancels the stylesheet",
			"attributes": {
				"style": {
					"spacing": {
						"margin": {
							"top": "0",
							"bottom": "0"
						}
					}
				}
			},
			"declarations": {
				"margin-top": "0",
				"margin-bottom": "0"
			}
		},
		{
			"name": "one axis only, the other left to the stylesheet",
			"attributes": {
				"style": {
					"spacing": {
						"margin": {
							"left": "8px",
							"right": "8px"
						}
					}
				}
			},
			"declarations": {
				"margin-left": "8px",
				"margin-right": "8px"
			}
		},
		{
			"name": "a full stroke",
